DevOps Interview Command Series — Prometheus (Day 13) 📊

Prometheus is the core monitoring & alerting system in cloud-native and Kubernetes environments.
It helps DevOps & SRE teams observe system health, performance, and reliability in real time.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Prometheus commands & queries you must know:

prometheus --version

systemctl start prometheus
systemctl status prometheus
systemctl restart prometheus

curl http://localhost:9090/metrics
curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/targets
curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/label/__name__/values

# PromQL (Very Important)
up
node_cpu_seconds_total
node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes
rate(node_cpu_seconds_total[5m])
sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total[5m])) by (pod)
histogram_quantile(0.95, rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m]))

# Alertmanager
amtool check-config alertmanager.yml
amtool alert

🎯 Interview Focus
• Pull-based monitoring model
• Exporters (node_exporter, kube-state-metrics)
• PromQL basics & aggregations
• Alert rules vs recording rules
• Monitoring vs observability
• Prometheus limitations & scalability
